WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.003
Pretty
remarkable breach of Russian air defenses

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:06.773
for a drone like that to fly all the way
across the country and hit the Kremlin.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.476
And the border is some 300 miles away.

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:12.112
So you have to imagine,
could they have seen it on radar?

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:15.215
Let's get answers to that
and much more with CNN military analyst

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:16.649
Colonel Cedric Leighton.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.785
Colonel Leighton,
before we get into that detail

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.820
about the distance
the drone may have flown.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.790
Let's take a look at this video
we've been watching over and over again

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.458
with your expert eyes.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:28.161
What do you see as the drone explodes
right there?

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:28.895
Yeah, right there.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.798
Boris,
what you're looking at is a direct hit.

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:36.002
So the anti-aircraft weaponry
that the Kremlin has deployed around it

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:40.673
for protection purposes, you know, is
clearly engaged in it seemed to my eyes,

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.243
it seems as if they knew exactly
what they were shooting at

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:46.646
and when that target
would be arriving in their area.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:47.814
Another thing

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:50.884
that's interesting, there are two people
apparently climbing this dome.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:55.055
And I also wanted to point out
there is a large stage in seating here.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:59.459
It's in anticipation
of May 9th victory day, a big symbolic day

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:04.097
for Russia, perhaps a day
that Ukraine might have wanted to target.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.100
Well, that's possible
because as you said, Boris,

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:11.171
you know, May 9th is a really big holiday
from a military perspective in Russia.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.406
This is where they show
a lot of their weaponry

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:16.309
have done so historically
ever since the end of World War Two.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:19.379
And you see the nine may nine May

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.216
signage
here, the Russian flag in the sands.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:26.986
All of this is getting ready
for a major military parade.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.890
And so from a symbolic perspective,
it would make sense for somebody to attack

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:31.891
something like this.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:36.129
But it also would be a perfect place
to mount a false flag operation.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.130
That is a good point.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:41.801
As we take another look, this is a new
angle of the drone exploding.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.269
You see it here in the upper left.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:46.739
And this view is important because
of the context, because of what you see.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.808
This is very close to Red Square.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:51.544
Saint Basil's
Cathedral is just off to the right there,

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:55.448
not far from a unknown situation,
cathedral as well.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.718
You imagine that this area
must be very well protected.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:01:59.752
Absolutely.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.722
And if we look at the map right
here, Red Square is right here.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:05.291
This is weird.
The parade would be taking place.

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:08.895
Annunciation Cathedral,
that's where the czars receive confession.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:12.031
There was their personal chapel
during the time of the czars.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:16.302
So that's a huge symbolic place
as far as Russia is concerned

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.837
that they would
obviously want to protect it.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.240
And Saint Basil's,
of course, is a very famous

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.142
part of the Kremlin structure itself.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:26.646
So to the point that Jim made
about the credulity of the Russian claim

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:29.916
that this was Ukraine
Let's pull up the map.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.719
This is some 300 miles away
from the Ukrainian border.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:35.722
You imagine that this drone didn't
even take off from here.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:40.026
Given what you know about Ukraine's
capabilities and Russia's capabilities

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:41.394
to see what's coming.

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.663
Does it seem likely
that this was a Ukrainian attack?

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:44.631
Unlikely.

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:47.300
From for that very reason,
because the Russians have radars

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.069
installations
all along this area right here.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.772
And the place where they would most likely

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.276
be launching something like this
from would be about here.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.879
And given that fact,
that's a little bit longer than 300 miles.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.047
It would take a lot of fuel.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.816
It would take longer in time
that some of these drones have.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:07.086
Now, it is possible
that Ukraine could have mounted

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:10.557
this operation from inside Russia
using special operations forces.

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:14.794
That is not beyond the realm
of possibility, but it is unlikely,

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.330
even though they have noted attacks
allegedly

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:21.868
against the areas in the South,
against airbases, things like that.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:25.638
So these are areas that can be targeted,
but it's very difficult to do that.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:29.309
And as President Selenski said,
they don't target the leadership.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:30.643
Russia does.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:33.513
Russia will use this as an excuse
to probably do something like that.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.182
But it is highly unlikely
that it came from Ukraine.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:39.219
And as far as we know, the U.S.,
the West, hasn't provided Ukraine

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:41.654
with that kind of equipment,
so it further strains credulity.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:43.890
Colonel Cedric
Leighton, always appreciate a perspective.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:44.791
Thank you so much for that.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:49.362
Ukraine denying any involvement
and accusing Moscow of a trick,

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:51.197
which begs several questions.

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:51.965
Be honest.

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:55.835
To be very frank with you,
what Ukraine first admit to it, Nick,

00:03:55.835 --> 00:04:00.206
if it was Ukraine, And what would it gain
from attacking the Kremlin?

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.377
The image

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:09.515
of these drones flying over the Kremlin
and one appearing to be shot down

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:14.554
or exploding right over the Kremlin
is an image of weakness for the Kremlin.

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:18.157
The Kremlin tries
to portray the war in Ukraine as something

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:24.597
that they're achieving all their goals,
that this is a special military operation,

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:30.470
a limited operation, not a full scale war,
something that really needs not worry

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:34.274
the Russian people
The fact that this incident happened over

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.144
the Kremlin tells
the Russian people that the Kremlin's

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.980
narrative isn't isn't correct.

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:44.951
That this is something
that that touches the Russian people,

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:48.721
because it's right over the Kremlin,
the heart of the heart of government.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:53.793
So the imagery tells the Russians
something that the Kremlin isn't

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:54.460
telling them.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:58.097
The question, of course,
and this is Ukraine's position, is that

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:00.266
this is imagery created by Russia

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.569
There is no evidence so far

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:07.040
to see physical evidence
to support Russia's claim

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.677
that this was an assassination
attempt on President Putin.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:14.814
And President Zelensky's
being very, very, very specific.

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:17.884
And I think we have to remember that
in these situations, people use words

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.419
quite carefully.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.821
He said we didn't attack Putin.

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.890
We didn't attack Putin.
We didn't attack Putin.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.825
We didn't attack Moscow.

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.194
When he talks about not

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:32.432
having ammunition, that's one of Ukraine's
ads and his narratives at the moment.

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:33.599
His in

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:37.870
Helsinki in Finland
meeting with Nordic allies and partners.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:41.741
And Ukraine is very concerned
that it doesn't have deep

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:45.511
enough stocks of ammunition
to really launch the kind of offensive

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:49.115
and sustain the offensive that it believes
it needs to that it needs to fight.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:52.852
So I think President Zelensky
message is on track

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.588
with that sort of messaging as well.

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:57.457
Where does it leave us?

00:05:57.457 --> 00:06:00.526
It leaves us in a situation
where the Kremlin has placed

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:04.864
a very, very high stakes,
if you will, on this,

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:08.801
because it's not just saying, well, some
drones from Ukraine flew over the Kremlin

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.770
and we took them down,
and no one was hurt.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:15.408
No, they're saying that this was
an assassination attempt on on President

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:21.047
Putin, which in the Russian playbook
potentially gives them the leverage

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:27.053
or the rationale to strike very
significantly at Ukraine's leadership.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.087
It's not clear,

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:31.891
but this has been often the way often
the way the Russian playbook works.

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:35.027
So, you know,
I think it's very difficult to analyze

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:38.564
precisely what happened, but precisely
what could happen because of it.

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:41.634
This playbook is open
and we've seen it used before.

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:42.668
Indeed.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:44.704
Nic Robertson
for us there in eastern Ukraine.

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:45.705
Thanks very much, Nic.

